---
import CalculatorLayout from '../../layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro';
---

<CalculatorLayout
  title="Right Triangle Area Calculator – Calculate Area of Right Triangle"
  description="Calculate the area of a right triangle from two legs, leg and hypotenuse, or side and acute angle with step-by-step mathematical formulas and conversions."
  category="Math"
  calculatorName="Right Triangle Area Calculator"
  slug="right-triangle-area-calculator"
  keywords={[
    'right triangle area calculator',
    'area of a right triangle calculator',
    'right triangle area',
    'right triangle area formula',
    'calculate right triangle area',
    'area of right angled triangle',
    'right triangle calculator',
    'triangle area calculator',
    'right triangle formula',
    'area from hypotenuse and angle',
    'area from two legs',
    '45 45 90 triangle area'
  ]}
>
  <div class="space-y-6">

    <!-- Calculator Card Container -->
    <div
      class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-linear-to-br from-white via-slate-50 to-blue-50/60 p-1.5 shadow-xl shadow-slate-900/5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:from-slate-950 dark:via-slate-950 dark:to-blue-950/20"
    >
      <!-- Top Mode Selector Tabs (Embedded in Card Border) -->
      <div
        class="flex items-center gap-1 border-b border-slate-300/80 px-2 pt-1 pb-0 dark:border-slate-800 overflow-x-auto scrollbar-thin"
      >
        <button
          type="button"
          id="tab-two-legs"
          data-mode="two_legs"
          class="mode-tab active rounded-t-xl border-t border-x border-slate-300/90 bg-white px-4 py-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 shadow-2xs -mb-px dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-white transition cursor-pointer shrink-0"
        >
          Two Legs (a, b)
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          id="tab-leg-hyp"
          data-mode="leg_hypotenuse"
          class="mode-tab rounded-t-xl bg-blue-700/90 px-4 py-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm font-bold text-white hover:bg-blue-800 dark:bg-blue-800 dark:hover:bg-blue-700 transition cursor-pointer shrink-0"
        >
          Leg &amp; Hypotenuse (a/b, c)
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          id="tab-hyp-angle"
          data-mode="hypotenuse_angle"
          class="mode-tab rounded-t-xl bg-blue-700/90 px-4 py-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm font-bold text-white hover:bg-blue-800 dark:bg-blue-800 dark:hover:bg-blue-700 transition cursor-pointer shrink-0"
        >
          Hypotenuse &amp; Angle (c, θ)
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          id="tab-leg-angle"
          data-mode="leg_angle"
          class="mode-tab rounded-t-xl bg-blue-700/90 px-4 py-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm font-bold text-white hover:bg-blue-800 dark:bg-blue-800 dark:hover:bg-blue-700 transition cursor-pointer shrink-0"
        >
          Leg &amp; Angle (a/b, θ)
        </button>
      </div>

      <!-- Main Form Container -->
      <form
        id="triangle-form"
        class="space-y-4 bg-white/45 p-4 sm:p-6 dark:bg-slate-950/40"
        novalidate
        onsubmit="return false;"
      >
        <!-- Mode Subtitle & Unit Selectors Bar -->
        <div
          class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 border-b border-slate-200/80 pb-3 dark:border-slate-800/80 text-xs"
        >
          <span id="mode-subtitle" class="font-bold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
            Known: Perpendicular Legs a and b
          </span>

          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
            <!-- Length Unit Selector -->
            <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5">
              <label for="select-unit" class="font-semibold text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Length Unit:</label>
              <select
                id="select-unit"
                class="rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-800 focus:border-blue-500 focus:outline-hidden dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer"
              >
                <option value="mm">Millimeters (mm)</option>
                <option value="cm" selected>Centimeters (cm)</option>
                <option value="m">Meters (m)</option>
                <option value="in">Inches (in)</option>
                <option value="ft">Feet (ft)</option>
                <option value="yd">Yards (yd)</option>
              </select>
            </div>

            <!-- Angle Unit Selector (Shown in angle modes) -->
            <div id="wrapper-angle-unit" class="hidden">
              <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5">
                <label for="select-angle-unit" class="font-semibold text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Angle Unit:</label>
                <select
                  id="select-angle-unit"
                  class="rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-800 focus:border-blue-500 focus:outline-hidden dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer"
                >
                  <option value="deg" selected>Degrees (°)</option>
                  <option value="rad">Radians (rad)</option>
                </select>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Dynamic Inputs Grid -->

        <!-- Row 1: Leg a -->
        <div
          id="row-leg-a"
          class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-[140px_1fr] items-center gap-2 sm:gap-4"
        >
          <label
            for="input-leg-a"
            class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white"
          >
            Leg a (Base)
          </label>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
            <div class="relative flex items-center w-40 sm:w-52">
              <input
                type="number"
                id="input-leg-a"
                value=""
                step="any"
                min="0"
                placeholder="Enter leg a"
                class="w-full rounded-lg border-2 border-slate-400/80 bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 shadow-2xs focus:border-blue-600 focus:outline-hidden dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-white pr-10"
                autocomplete="off"
              />
              <span class="unit-badge pointer-events-none absolute right-3 text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-medium">cm</span>
            </div>
            <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">horizontal perpendicular leg</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Row 2: Leg b -->
        <div
          id="row-leg-b"
          class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-[140px_1fr] items-center gap-2 sm:gap-4"
        >
          <label
            for="input-leg-b"
            class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white"
          >
            Leg b (Height)
          </label>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
            <div class="relative flex items-center w-40 sm:w-52">
              <input
                type="number"
                id="input-leg-b"
                value=""
                step="any"
                min="0"
                placeholder="Enter leg b"
                class="w-full rounded-lg border-2 border-slate-400/80 bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 shadow-2xs focus:border-blue-600 focus:outline-hidden dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-white pr-10"
                autocomplete="off"
              />
              <span class="unit-badge pointer-events-none absolute right-3 text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-medium">cm</span>
            </div>
            <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">vertical perpendicular leg</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Row 3: Leg Choice (Used in Leg & Hypotenuse / Leg & Angle modes) -->
        <div id="row-leg-choice" class="hidden">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-[140px_1fr] items-center gap-2 sm:gap-4">
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Known Leg</span>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 text-xs font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
              <label class="flex items-center gap-1.5 cursor-pointer">
                <input type="radio" name="known-leg" value="a" checked class="text-blue-600 focus:ring-blue-500 cursor-pointer" />
                <span>Leg a (Base)</span>
              </label>
              <label class="flex items-center gap-1.5 cursor-pointer">
                <input type="radio" name="known-leg" value="b" class="text-blue-600 focus:ring-blue-500 cursor-pointer" />
                <span>Leg b (Height)</span>
              </label>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Row 4: Single Leg Input (Used when known-leg radio is selected) -->
        <div id="row-single-leg" class="hidden">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-[140px_1fr] items-center gap-2 sm:gap-4">
            <label
              for="input-single-leg"
              id="label-single-leg"
              class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white"
            >
              Leg a Length
            </label>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
              <div class="relative flex items-center w-40 sm:w-52">
                <input
                  type="number"
                  id="input-single-leg"
                  value=""
                  step="any"
                  min="0"
                  placeholder="Enter leg length"
                  class="w-full rounded-lg border-2 border-slate-400/80 bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 shadow-2xs focus:border-blue-600 focus:outline-hidden dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-white pr-10"
                  autocomplete="off"
                />
                <span class="unit-badge pointer-events-none absolute right-3 text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-medium">cm</span>
              </div>
              <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">perpendicular side</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Row 5: Hypotenuse c -->
        <div id="row-hypotenuse" class="hidden">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-[140px_1fr] items-center gap-2 sm:gap-4">
            <label
              for="input-hypotenuse"
              class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white"
            >
              Hypotenuse (c)
            </label>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
              <div class="relative flex items-center w-40 sm:w-52">
                <input
                  type="number"
                  id="input-hypotenuse"
                  value=""
                  step="any"
                  min="0"
                  placeholder="Enter hypotenuse c"
                  class="w-full rounded-lg border-2 border-slate-400/80 bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 shadow-2xs focus:border-blue-600 focus:outline-hidden dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-white pr-10"
                  autocomplete="off"
                />
                <span class="unit-badge pointer-events-none absolute right-3 text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-medium">cm</span>
              </div>
              <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">longest side opposite 90° angle (c &gt; leg)</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Row 6: Angle Type Selector (Alpha vs Beta) -->
        <div id="row-angle-type" class="hidden">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-[140px_1fr] items-center gap-2 sm:gap-4">
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Known Angle</span>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 text-xs font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
              <label class="flex items-center gap-1.5 cursor-pointer">
                <input type="radio" name="angle-type" value="alpha" checked class="text-blue-600 focus:ring-blue-500 cursor-pointer" />
                <span>Angle α (opposite leg a)</span>
              </label>
              <label class="flex items-center gap-1.5 cursor-pointer">
                <input type="radio" name="angle-type" value="beta" class="text-blue-600 focus:ring-blue-500 cursor-pointer" />
                <span>Angle β (opposite leg b)</span>
              </label>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Row 7: Angle Input -->
        <div id="row-angle-val" class="hidden">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-[140px_1fr] items-center gap-2 sm:gap-4">
            <label
              for="input-angle-val"
              id="label-angle-val"
              class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white"
            >
              Acute Angle (α)
            </label>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
              <div class="relative flex items-center w-40 sm:w-52">
                <input
                  type="number"
                  id="input-angle-val"
                  value=""
                  step="any"
                  min="0"
                  max="90"
                  placeholder="e.g. 30 or 45"
                  class="w-full rounded-lg border-2 border-slate-400/80 bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 shadow-2xs focus:border-blue-600 focus:outline-hidden dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-white pr-10"
                  autocomplete="off"
                />
                <span id="badge-angle-unit" class="pointer-events-none absolute right-3 text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-bold">°</span>
              </div>
              <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">must be strictly between 0° and 90°</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Row 8: Action Buttons (Green Calculate & Gray Clear) -->
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 pt-3">
          <button
            type="submit"
            id="btn-calculate"
            class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-emerald-600 px-6 py-2.5 text-sm font-extrabold text-white shadow-lg shadow-emerald-600/20 transition hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:bg-emerald-700 active:scale-[0.98] cursor-pointer"
          >
            <span>Calculate</span>
            <span class="flex h-5 w-5 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-white/20 text-[10px]">
              ▶
            </span>
          </button>
          <button
            type="button"
            id="btn-clear"
            class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-slate-400 hover:bg-slate-500 dark:bg-slate-600 dark:hover:bg-slate-500 px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-white shadow-sm active:scale-[0.98] transition cursor-pointer"
          >
            Clear
          </button>
        </div>

        <!-- Error Banner -->
        <p
          id="triangle-error"
          class="hidden rounded-xl border border-red-200 bg-red-50 px-3 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-red-700 dark:border-red-900/60 dark:bg-red-950/30 dark:text-red-300"
          role="alert"
          aria-live="polite"
        >
        </p>
      </form>
    </div>

    <!-- Initial Prompt Placeholder (Shown before Calculate is clicked) -->
    <div
      id="results-placeholder"
      class="rounded-2xl border border-dashed border-slate-300 bg-slate-50/60 p-8 text-center dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/40"
    >
      <div
        class="mx-auto flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-100 text-xl text-blue-700 dark:bg-blue-950 dark:text-blue-300"
      >
        📐
      </div>
      <h3 class="mt-3 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
        Ready to Calculate Right Triangle Area
      </h3>
      <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 max-w-md mx-auto">
        Select your known measurements above, enter your values into the empty fields, and click the green <strong>"Calculate ▶"</strong> button to view the area, missing sides, perimeter, and step-by-step derivation.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Calculation Results Card (Revealed on Calculate) -->
    <div
      id="results-card"
      class="hidden rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/95 p-5 shadow-xs transition dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/90 sm:p-6 space-y-6"
    >
      <!-- Top Banner: Primary Area -->
      <div
        class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-4 border-b border-slate-200 pb-5 dark:border-slate-800"
      >
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
              Right Triangle Area (A)
            </span>
            <span
              id="res-special-tag"
              class="hidden rounded-full bg-emerald-100 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-bold text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-950 dark:text-emerald-300"
            >
              45°-45°-90° Isosceles
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-2">
            <span
              id="res-area-val"
              class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-black tracking-tight text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400"
            >
              —
            </span>
            <span
              id="res-area-unit"
              class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400"
            >
              cm²
            </span>
          </div>
          <p id="res-subtitle" class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
            Calculated from perpendicular base and height
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Quick Summary Stats -->
        <div class="flex sm:flex-col items-start sm:items-end justify-between gap-1 text-xs">
          <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
            Perimeter (P): <span id="res-perimeter" class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">—</span>
          </div>
          <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
            Hypotenuse (c): <span id="res-hypotenuse-stat" class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">—</span>
          </div>
          <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
            Altitude to Hypotenuse (h_c): <span id="res-altitude" class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">—</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Grid of Side Lengths & Angles -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3 text-xs">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200/80 bg-white p-3 shadow-2xs dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
          <span class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 block font-medium">Leg a (Base):</span>
          <span id="stat-leg-a" class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white text-sm mt-0.5 block">—</span>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200/80 bg-white p-3 shadow-2xs dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
          <span class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 block font-medium">Leg b (Height):</span>
          <span id="stat-leg-b" class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white text-sm mt-0.5 block">—</span>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200/80 bg-white p-3 shadow-2xs dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
          <span class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 block font-medium">Angle α (opp a):</span>
          <span id="stat-angle-alpha" class="font-bold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 text-sm mt-0.5 block">—</span>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200/80 bg-white p-3 shadow-2xs dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
          <span class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 block font-medium">Angle β (opp b):</span>
          <span id="stat-angle-beta" class="font-bold text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 text-sm mt-0.5 block">—</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Live Interactive Proportional Triangle SVG Preview -->
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
          <h4 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 flex items-center gap-1.5">
            <span>📐</span> Proportional Right Triangle Diagram
          </h4>
          <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">Euclidean Scale</span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-center p-2">
          <svg id="svg-triangle-preview" viewBox="0 0 360 220" class="w-full max-w-sm h-48 sm:h-56">
            <!-- Triangle Polygon -->
            <polygon id="svg-poly" points="60,180 60,40 300,180" fill="rgba(37,99,235,0.12)" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linejoin="round" />
            <!-- Right Angle Square Marker -->
            <path id="svg-right-box" d="M 60 162 L 78 162 L 78 180" fill="none" stroke="#1e40af" stroke-width="2" />
            <circle id="svg-right-dot" cx="69" cy="171" r="2" fill="#1e40af" />
            <!-- Labels -->
            <text id="svg-label-a" x="180" y="202" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f172a" text-anchor="middle">a = 6</text>
            <text id="svg-label-b" x="42" y="115" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f172a" text-anchor="middle">b = 8</text>
            <text id="svg-label-c" x="195" y="100" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#2563eb" text-anchor="middle">c = 10</text>
            <text id="svg-label-alpha" x="265" y="174" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="10" font-weight="bold" fill="#d97706" text-anchor="end">α</text>
            <text id="svg-label-beta" x="72" y="65" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="10" font-weight="bold" fill="#059669" text-anchor="start">β</text>
          </svg>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Step-by-Step Mathematical Derivation -->
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
        <h4 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <span>📝</span> Step-by-Step Calculation Breakdown
        </h4>
        <ol id="res-steps" class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 list-decimal pl-5 font-mono leading-relaxed">
        </ol>
      </div>

      <!-- Area in Other Standard Units Table -->
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 overflow-x-auto">
        <h4 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 mb-3 flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <span>🔄</span> Equivalent Area in Other Units
        </h4>
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs font-mono">
          <tbody id="table-units-body" class="divide-y divide-slate-100 dark:divide-slate-800 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ======================================================== -->
  <!-- EDUCATIONAL CONTENT & COMPREHENSIVE GUIDE                -->
  <!-- ======================================================== -->
  <Fragment slot="content">
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">What Is a Right Triangle?</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3 mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          A <strong>right triangle</strong> (also called a <em>right-angled triangle</em>) is a fundamental geometric polygon characterized by having exactly one interior angle measuring <strong>90 degrees (90°)</strong>, known as the right angle. In any Euclidean flat plane, the sum of all three interior angles in a triangle always equals 180°. Because one angle is fixed at 90°, the remaining two acute angles (designated as <em>α</em> and <em>β</em>) are strictly complementary:
        </p>
        <div class="my-3 rounded-2xl border border-blue-200 bg-blue-50/50 p-4 font-mono text-center text-base sm:text-lg font-black text-blue-700 dark:border-blue-900/60 dark:bg-blue-950/40 dark:text-blue-300">
          α + β = 90° &nbsp;&nbsp;(or&nbsp; π / 2 &nbsp;radians)
        </div>
        <p>
          The two sides that meet to form the 90° angle are called the <strong>legs</strong> (or catheti), denoted as <em>a</em> and <em>b</em>. The third side, positioned directly across from the right angle, is the <strong>hypotenuse</strong> (<em>c</em>), which is always the longest side of the right triangle.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Educational Diagram 1: Basic Right Triangle -->
    <div class="my-6 text-center">
      <img
        src="/images/math/right-triangle-area-formula.svg"
        alt="Right triangle diagram illustrating perpendicular legs a and b, hypotenuse c, right angle marker, and area formula A = 1/2 * a * b"
        class="mx-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 shadow-sm max-w-full sm:max-w-md"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-medium">
        Figure 1: Anatomy of a right triangle with perpendicular legs (base <em>a</em> and height <em>b</em>), hypotenuse <em>c</em>, and the core area relation.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">The Fundamental Right Triangle Area Formula</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3 mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          For any general triangle, the area is calculated as half the base multiplied by the perpendicular height: <code>Area = ½ × base × height</code>. In a right triangle, the two perpendicular legs form their own mutual altitude. Therefore, one leg can be designated as the horizontal base (<em>a</em>) and the other leg serves directly as the perpendicular height (<em>b</em>):
        </p>
        <div class="my-3 rounded-2xl border border-blue-200 bg-blue-50/50 p-4 font-mono text-center text-base sm:text-lg font-black text-blue-700 dark:border-blue-900/60 dark:bg-blue-950/40 dark:text-blue-300">
          Area = (a × b) / 2
        </div>
        <p>
          <strong>Why is this formula true?</strong> Geometrically, if you construct a rectangle with side lengths <em>a</em> and <em>b</em>, drawing a diagonal line from one corner to the opposite corner splits the rectangle into two identical, congruent right triangles. The area of the entire rectangle is <code>a × b</code>, so each individual right triangle possesses exactly half of that rectangular area.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Calculating Area from One Leg and the Hypotenuse</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3 mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          When you know the hypotenuse <em>c</em> and only one leg (say leg <em>a</em>), the Pythagorean theorem enables you to compute the missing perpendicular leg <em>b</em>:
        </p>
        <div class="my-2 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/80 p-3 font-mono text-sm dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
          a² + b² = c² &nbsp;⟹&nbsp; b = √(c² − a²)
        </div>
        <p>
          Once leg <em>b</em> is determined, substituting it into the primary area formula yields:
        </p>
        <div class="my-2 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/80 p-3 font-mono text-sm dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
          Area = [a × √(c² − a²)] / 2
        </div>
        <p>
          Similarly, if leg <em>b</em> and hypotenuse <em>c</em> are given, the equation becomes <code>Area = [b × √(c² − b²)] / 2</code>.
        </p>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
          <strong>Geometric Constraint:</strong> Because the hypotenuse is the longest side, the condition <code>c &gt; a &gt; 0</code> must always hold true. If <em>c ≤ a</em>, the quantity under the radical <code>c² − a²</code> becomes zero or negative, making a valid Euclidean right triangle impossible.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Educational Diagram 2: Hypotenuse and Angle -->
    <div class="my-6 text-center">
      <img
        src="/images/math/right-triangle-angle-area.svg"
        alt="Trigonometric right triangle diagram showing hypotenuse c, acute angles alpha and beta, and sine cosine projection formulas"
        class="mx-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 shadow-sm max-w-full sm:max-w-md"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-medium">
        Figure 2: Trigonometric decomposition of legs using acute angles <em>α</em> and <em>β</em>, where <em>a = c · sin(α)</em> and <em>b = c · cos(α)</em>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Calculating Area from the Hypotenuse and an Acute Angle</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3 mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          If you only have the hypotenuse <em>c</em> and one acute angle (for example, angle <em>α</em> opposite leg <em>a</em>), you can resolve both perpendicular legs using basic trigonometric sine and cosine functions:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-1.5 list-disc list-inside">
          <li><code>sin(α) = a / c ⟹ a = c × sin(α)</code></li>
          <li><code>cos(α) = b / c ⟹ b = c × cos(α)</code></li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Substituting these definitions directly into the area formula gives the elegant trigonometric equation:
        </p>
        <div class="my-3 rounded-2xl border border-blue-200 bg-blue-50/50 p-4 font-mono text-center text-base sm:text-lg font-black text-blue-700 dark:border-blue-900/60 dark:bg-blue-950/40 dark:text-blue-300">
          Area = [c² × sin(α) × cos(α)] / 2
        </div>
        <p>
          Using the trigonometric double-angle identity <code>2 × sin(α) × cos(α) = sin(2α)</code>, this formula simplifies even further to:
        </p>
        <div class="my-2 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/80 p-3 font-mono text-sm text-center dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
          Area = [c² × sin(2α)] / 4
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Calculating Area from One Leg and an Acute Angle</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3 mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          When you know one leg and an acute angle, the <strong>tangent</strong> ratio relates the two perpendicular sides:
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mt-2">
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/50 p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/40">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Given Leg a and Opposite Angle α:</h3>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 font-mono">
              tan(α) = a / b ⟹ b = a / tan(α)
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-xs font-mono font-bold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">
              Area = a² / [2 × tan(α)]
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/50 p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/40">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Given Leg b and Adjacent Angle α:</h3>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 font-mono">
              tan(α) = a / b ⟹ a = b × tan(α)
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-xs font-mono font-bold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">
              Area = [b² × tan(α)] / 2
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Educational Diagram 3: 45-45-90 Triangle -->
    <div class="my-6 text-center">
      <img
        src="/images/math/45-45-90-triangle.svg"
        alt="45 45 90 isosceles right triangle diagram with equal legs x, hypotenuse x sqrt 2, and area formulas"
        class="mx-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 shadow-sm max-w-full sm:max-w-md"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-medium">
        Figure 3: Special 45°-45°-90° isosceles right triangle where both legs are equal (<em>a = b</em>) and the hypotenuse is <em>c = a√2</em>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">The Special 45°-45°-90° Isosceles Right Triangle</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3 mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          A particularly notable right triangle is the <strong>45°-45°-90° triangle</strong>, also known as the <em>isosceles right triangle</em>. In this configuration, both acute angles equal 45° (<em>α = β = 45°</em>). Because equal angles subtend equal sides, both perpendicular legs are identical in length:
        </p>
        <div class="my-2 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/80 p-3 font-mono text-sm dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
          a = b &nbsp;&nbsp;and&nbsp;&nbsp; c = a√2 ≈ 1.4142 × a
        </div>
        <p>
          Its area can be formulated in two remarkably compact ways:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-1.5 list-disc list-inside">
          <li><strong>Using the leg length:</strong> <code>Area = a² / 2</code></li>
          <li><strong>Using the hypotenuse length:</strong> <code>Area = c² / 4</code></li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          This triangle represents exactly one-half of a square cut diagonally across its vertices. If a square has side length <em>a</em>, its full area is <code>a²</code>, confirming that the 45°-45°-90° right triangle has an area of exactly <code>a² / 2</code>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Worked Mathematical Examples</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/60 p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Example 1: Two Known Legs (3-4-5 Triangle)</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            A construction triangle has perpendicular legs measuring <strong>a = 3 m</strong> and <strong>b = 4 m</strong>.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 space-y-1">
            <div>• Area = (a × b) / 2 = (3 × 4) / 2 = 12 / 2 = <strong>6 m²</strong></div>
            <div>• Hypotenuse c = √(3² + 4²) = √(9 + 16) = √25 = <strong>5 m</strong></div>
            <div>• Perimeter P = 3 + 4 + 5 = <strong>12 m</strong></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/60 p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Example 2: Leg and Hypotenuse (a = 6 in, c = 10 in)</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            A wooden rafter has leg <strong>a = 6 in</strong> and hypotenuse <strong>c = 10 in</strong>.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 space-y-1">
            <div>• Missing leg b = √(c² − a²) = √(10² − 6²) = √(100 − 36) = √64 = <strong>8 in</strong></div>
            <div>• Area = (6 × 8) / 2 = 48 / 2 = <strong>24 in²</strong></div>
            <div>• Angle α = arcsin(6 / 10) = arcsin(0.6) ≈ <strong>36.87°</strong></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/60 p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Example 3: Hypotenuse and 30° Acute Angle (c = 12 cm, α = 30°)</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            An architect drafts a roof section with hypotenuse <strong>c = 12 cm</strong> and pitch <strong>α = 30°</strong>.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 space-y-1">
            <div>• Leg a = c × sin(30°) = 12 × 0.5 = <strong>6 cm</strong></div>
            <div>• Leg b = c × cos(30°) = 12 × (√3 / 2) ≈ 12 × 0.866025 = <strong>10.3923 cm</strong></div>
            <div>• Area = (6 × 10.3923) / 2 ≈ <strong>31.1769 cm²</strong></div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Common Mistakes in Right Triangle Calculations</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 mt-3 text-xs text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/60 p-3.5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950">
          <strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white block mb-1">❌ Confusing Hypotenuse with a Leg:</strong>
          Multiplying a leg by the hypotenuse directly (e.g. <code>c × a / 2</code>) will overestimate the area. The two sides multiplied in the numerator must be perpendicular to each other.
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/60 p-3.5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950">
          <strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white block mb-1">❌ Forgetting to Divide by 2:</strong>
          Calculating <code>a × b</code> without halving computes the area of the full bounding rectangle, doubling the true triangle area.
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/60 p-3.5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950">
          <strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white block mb-1">❌ Setting Hypotenuse Shorter Than a Leg:</strong>
          In Euclidean geometry, the hypotenuse is always strictly the longest side. Providing <code>c ≤ a</code> causes the square root calculation <code>√(c² − a²)</code> to evaluate an impossible negative radicand.
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/60 p-3.5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950">
          <strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white block mb-1">❌ Entering 90° as an Acute Angle:</strong>
          The right angle is already 90°. The remaining two acute angles must each be strictly between 0° and 90°.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Related Math &amp; Geometry Calculators</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
        Explore our companion precision mathematical and geometry tools:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 list-disc list-inside">
